Z||000000||firstfiero||05-10-2001||09:18 AM||||     I just read that mazda made a mistake with the miata this year. They advertised the new one was increased to like 175 hp and when the car mags. got it they found it to be slower then the previous year. Mazda checked it out and figured out that the dyno numbers they were giving were befor they added all the amercian hp robbing crap that has to go on all cars...damn emmissions!!. Any way for this they have told all the miata owners that if you don't want your car they will give you a full refund. If you keep the car they'll give you free service for the life of the car and a $500 credit card to spend on anything mazda has. If only gm treated their customers like this maybe...just maybe they would have sold better and would have stuck around a little longer. At the very least their rep. would be a hell of alot better!<P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">         <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||8
Z||000001||Raydar||05-10-2001||09:27 AM||||Japanese automakers are famous for this. If they realize they screwed up, they go to extremes to satisfy their customers. Of course they do it for the good press they'll receive, too.<BR>Has a lot to do with why the Japanese automakers beat the US like a mule for so many years. Our quality is catching up rapidly, but our customer service still is third-rate. IMHO.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000002||WampusCat||05-10-2001||09:56 AM||||I bought a used '92 Toyota PU in '96 with 60k miles on it.  It developed an A/C leak at 96k and when I took it to a Dealer for service, they told me there was a bulletin to replace the head gaskets.  I told them the truck was running fine but they wanted to replace them anyway because a high percentage had failed on the 3.0.  While they had the heads off, they found some parts "out of spec" so they replaced the rings, bearings, and other stuff, all for free on a truck with 96k miles that I had bought used from an individual.  I just can't imagine a Detroit company doing that.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Slammed Fiero||05-10-2001||10:20 AM||||GM Does handle things like this , if they handled things like mazda , they would be mostly owned by Ford , just like Mazda is. A full loaded miata here is a tad over 40 GRAND!!<P>I still have the letter From 1969 from GM saying that in light of the cancellation of the Corvair GM is offering a $300 allowance towards (yes $300 in 69) the purchase of any new GM vehicle. This was based on the purchase of a 1969 Garnet red , fully loaded Corvair COnvert (red , white top , black interior, 4spd , 140hp , power top ..everything!!). The car has since turned over 36,000 miles , Was bought right off the floor from the 1969 Toronto autoshow where it was displayed.<P>#494 of 521 convertibiles built in 1969.<BR>Built the last week of production of the Corvair.<P>On a side note , all 69 converts were hand built on dollies in the corner of the factory, compared to our 66 Corsas it has a few flaws with gaps and what not. <BR>JM<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 05-10-2001).]||||reg||1
