Z||000008||Raydar||05-10-2001||11:37 AM||||The Georgia Fiero club has done some events -picnics and such- with one of the local Corvair clubs. It seems to me that we have a great deal in common: <P>1. We own discontinued, orphaned GM cars.<BR>2. We, and our cars, are greatly misunderstood by the vast majority of people.<BR>3. The cars are both "unconventional", in terms of drivetrain.<BR>4. The owners are generally just a bit eccentric, as well.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>And to keep this on topic, <BR>I had a roommate that had an 84 RX7, purchased new. It was a blast to drive. Redline happened very quickly, and the rotary engine was silky smooth. No vibration at all.<BR>He sold it only about two years ago, to a teenager who promptly blew out the apex seals.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 05-10-2001).]||||reg||1
